# fixedbugs, defect 2467, lane b31-ffi, 2026-11-11: `own.h` declares the
# variadic `v2467` and defines it again as a macro of two arguments, as
# `curl/curl.h` does `curl_easy_setopt`, so that a call passes exactly two.
# The declaration gives one, its result right: every call this program's C
# writes of it goes through the macro, which refuses it. Until this defect it
# was told *returns `int (int, ...)`*, the function's type clang names once
# it has refused the macro's invocation, as the result's; this line is its
# mark.
extern "own.h"
    function v2467(a: i32) -> i32  #~ ffi_macro_name

function main()
    print(v2467(a: 1))
